WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.117 --> 00:00:17.102
On a golden summer afternoon, Alice sat by the river.

2
00:00:17.943 --> 00:00:21.804
Her older sister, Charlotte, sat beside her, happily reading a book.

3
00:00:22.825 --> 00:00:26.106
Feeling bored, Alice glanced at her sister's book.

4
00:00:27.047 --> 00:00:29.167
"What's the point of a book without pictures?"

5
00:00:29.608 --> 00:00:30.308
Alice asked.

6
00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:34.382
Charlotte was too busy reading to reply.

7
00:00:37.664 --> 00:00:42.007
Alice gave a tired sigh and thought about making a daisy chain.

8
00:00:42.767 --> 00:00:46.030
However, that would require getting up to pick the daisies.

9
00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:50.993
And the hot day was making Alice feel very tired and lazy.

10
00:00:52.314 --> 00:00:55.476
Suddenly a rabbit ran past the two girls.

11
00:00:56.657 --> 00:00:59.139
He was white and wore a colorful vest.

12
00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:00.239
"Oh, dear!

13
00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:01.000
Oh, dear!"

14
00:01:01.376 --> 00:01:01.877
he cried.

15
00:01:01.897 --> 00:01:03.658
"I'm going to be late!"

16
00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:10.364
Alice was so sleepy that she didn't think a talking animal was strange.

17
00:01:11.365 --> 00:01:15.208
But then the White Rabbit pulled a watch from his vest pocket.

18
00:01:18.931 --> 00:01:21.413
don't wear vests," Alice said to herself.

19
00:01:21.433 --> 00:01:24.496
"And they certainly don't carry watches."

20
00:01:26.477 --> 00:01:29.360
Alice jumped up and ran after the White Rabbit.

21
00:01:30.652 --> 00:01:33.974
Near a hedge he popped down a large rabbit hole.

22
00:01:34.915 --> 00:01:38.997
Alice followed right after him, not thinking about how she'd get out.

23
00:01:40.278 --> 00:01:41.838
Suddenly she was falling!

24
00:01:41.858 --> 00:01:44.680
"Help!" Alice cried.

25
00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:48.902
She felt as if she were falling down a deep well.

26
00:01:49.783 --> 00:01:54.505
It was too dark to see anything below, so Alice looked around as she fell.

27
00:01:55.626 --> 00:01:58.668
The rabbit hole was lined with cupboards and shelves.

28
00:01:59.724 --> 00:02:02.206
Maps and pictures decorated the walls.

29
00:02:03.848 --> 00:02:07.411
Alice grabbed a jar labeled Orange Jam from one shelf.

30
00:02:09.333 --> 00:02:11.735
She was disappointed to discover it was empty.

31
00:02:11.755 --> 00:02:18.821
"If I drop this jar, it might kill somebody below," Alice said.

32
00:02:20.242 --> 00:02:23.064
She slipped it onto the next shelf she passed.

33
00:02:24.265 --> 00:02:25.807
Alice continued to fall.

34
00:02:25.827 --> 00:02:30.433
"After this, I'll never get upset about just falling down some stairs.

35
00:02:31.313 --> 00:02:34.034
Why, I won't even complain if I fall off the roof!"

36
00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:36.795
Down, down, down.

37
00:02:37.535 --> 00:02:39.315
Would this fall ever end?

38
00:02:43.517 --> 00:02:45.277
many miles have I fallen by now?"

39
00:02:45.657 --> 00:02:46.197
Alice said.

40
00:02:46.217 --> 00:02:49.758
"I must be getting near the center of the earth.

41
00:02:50.539 --> 00:02:52.599
What if I fall right through the earth?"

42
00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:54.760
Where would she end up?

43
00:02:55.944 --> 00:02:58.585
Alice tried to remember her geography lessons.

44
00:02:58.605 --> 00:03:01.787
"I'll just have to ask the first person I meet.

45
00:03:02.467 --> 00:03:05.908
I'll say, 'Please, ma'am, is this New Zealand or Australia?'"

46
00:03:07.269 --> 00:03:12.351
Alice was silent for a while, but then she started thinking about Dinah, her cat.

47
00:03:12.371 --> 00:03:16.873
"I hope someone remembers to feed Dinah tonight," Alice said aloud.

48
00:03:16.893 --> 00:03:19.754
"Oh, Dinah, I wish you were here!

49
00:03:20.575 --> 00:03:23.236
There aren't any mice in the air, but you might catch a bat.

50
00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:26.041
Do cats eat bats?

51
00:03:27.022 --> 00:03:28.463
Do bats eat cats?"

52
00:03:29.684 --> 00:03:32.126
Alice didn't know the answer to either question.

53
00:03:33.127 --> 00:03:35.710
And she was feeling so, so tired.

54
00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:42.295
She was beginning to dream that she was walking hand in hand with Dinah— Thump!

55
00:03:43.136 --> 00:03:47.080
Suddenly Alice landed on a pile of sticks and dry leaves.

56
00:03:49.001 --> 00:03:51.604
She wasn't hurt, so she jumped right up.

57
00:03:52.496 --> 00:03:56.158
Ahead, the White Rabbit was hurrying down a long passage.

58
00:03:56.178 --> 00:03:58.659
"I'd better catch up with that rabbit!"

59
00:03:59.320 --> 00:04:01.521
Alice ran as fast as she could.

60
00:04:01.541 --> 00:04:05.043
"Oh, my ears and whiskers!

61
00:04:05.723 --> 00:04:07.164
It's getting very late!"

62
00:04:07.524 --> 00:04:09.625
the White Rabbit said as he turned a corner.

63
00:04:11.466 --> 00:04:15.689
Alice turned the corner too, but the White Rabbit had disappeared.

64
00:04:16.709 --> 00:04:21.212
She was now in a long, low hall with doors lining both walls.

65
00:04:22.108 --> 00:04:25.430
Lamps hanging from the ceiling dimly illuminated the hall.

66
00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:30.393
"The White Rabbit must have gone through one of these doors," Alice said.

67
00:04:31.974 --> 00:04:35.355
She walked down one side of the hall, trying every door.

68
00:04:36.856 --> 00:04:38.037
They were all locked.

69
00:04:39.678 --> 00:04:41.339
She walked up the other side of the hall.

70
00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:44.921
Those doors were locked too.

71
00:04:47.822 --> 00:04:50.264
Alice stood sadly in the middle of the hall.

72
00:04:51.265 --> 00:04:52.877
"How will I ever get out of here?"

73
00:04:53.461 --> 00:04:54.046
she cried.
